From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Open Video Tools contributors <noreply@ovt.dev>
Date: 2026-11-14
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] inspection: snapshot the frame before each in-loop filter

While an inspection callback is set, av1_decode_tg_tiles_and_wrapup()
copies the frame buffer before deblocking, before CDEF and before loop
restoration (after super-resolution). insp_frame_data.snapshots[] points
at the copies, which the decoder owns and reuses for the next frame.
Frames whose filters are skipped (IntraBC, single-tile decoding) get the
same picture in all three snapshots.

The copies are tight (stride = width * bytes per sample) and are made only
when inspect_cb != NULL, so a decoder without an inspection callback does
no extra work; without CONFIG_INSPECTION the snapshot points compile to
nothing.

Upstream-Status: Pending [to be submitted to aomedia-review.googlesource.com by OVT WI-2.160]
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 The Open Video Tools contributors
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
Rationale: the decoder filters the frame in place, so the pre-filter pictures exist only inside
  av1_decode_tg_tiles_and_wrapup(); no API or control returns them.
---
